WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.652
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:09.524
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:16.819
Unit twenty-four: Present Perfect with Ever / Never. Today you will ask and talk about life experiences.

4
00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:19.748
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.049
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:25.641
Ever.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.917
Ever means at any time in your life.

8
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:30.901
Have you ever travelled?

9
00:00:31.517 --> 00:00:33.705
Your turn. Say: Ever.

10
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.394
Ever.

11
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:38.884
Never.

12
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:41.802
Never means not at any time.

13
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.812
I have never flown.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.953
Your turn. Say: Never.

15
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:50.708
Never.

16
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.509
Have been.

17
00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:55.551
Have been means have visited a place.

18
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.697
I have been to Japan.

19
00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.901
Your turn. Say: Have been.

20
00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:04.907
Have been.

21
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.605
Have tried.

22
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:09.639
Have tried means have tested something.

23
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.507
I have tried durian.

24
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:14.560
Your turn. Say: Have tried.

25
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.482
Have tried.

26
00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:20.334
Experience.

27
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.559
Experience means something that you have done.

28
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.871
It was a great experience.

29
00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:29.101
Your turn. Say: Experience.

30
00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:33.281
Experience.

31
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:34.797
Before.

32
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:37.725
Before means earlier than now.

33
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:39.910
I have seen it before.

34
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.612
Your turn. Say: Before.

35
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:46.224
Before.

36
00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:47.787
Once.

37
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:50.446
Once means one time.

38
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.643
I have been there once.

39
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.647
Your turn. Say: Once.

40
00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.455
Once.

41
00:02:00.217 --> 00:02:01.067
Twice.

42
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.851
Twice means two times.

43
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.974
I have seen it twice.

44
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.282
Your turn. Say: Twice.

45
00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.274
Twice.

46
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:18.101
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.205
Visal, have you ever tried durian?

48
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:32.823
Yes, I have. I have tried it twice. We use have you ever + past participle to ask about life experience. The time is not important.

49
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:34.976
And never?

50
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:46.169
Never means not at any time: I have never been to Japan. Never is already negative, so we use a positive verb. Do not say I haven't never been.

51
00:02:47.283 --> 00:02:49.132
How do we say how many times?

52
00:02:50.217 --> 00:03:01.962
Once, twice, three times: I have been to Siem Reap three times. Been means visited and come back. Gone means still there: She has gone to Japan, so she is not here.

53
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.809
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:10.540
Grammar focus: Present perfect: ever and never plus past participle.

55
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.016
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.717 --> 00:03:14.356
Have you ever tried durian?

57
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.913
I have never been to Japan.

58
00:03:17.817 --> 00:03:19.375
I have seen it twice.

59
00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:28.480
Ask Have you ever + past participle? and answer with have / haven't or never. Been = visited and returned; gone = still away.

60
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:32.519
Be careful! Don't say: I haven't never tried it.

61
00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.571
Say: I have never tried it.

62
00:03:36.871 --> 00:03:38.545
Never is already negative.

63
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:41.777
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:43.823
Ever and Never.

65
00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:47.240
Have you ever tried durian? I have tried it twice.

66
00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:50.709
I have never been to Japan, but I want to go.

67
00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.152
My brother has been to Siem Reap three times.

68
00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:57.874
She has gone to Japan, so she is not at home.

69
00:03:58.867 --> 00:04:01.052
Experience teaches us about the world.

70
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.913
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.784
Have you blank eaten sushi?

72
00:04:09.084 --> 00:04:12.401
A, ever. B, yet. C, never.

73
00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:18.094
The answer is A: ever.

74
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.971
I have blank seen a tiger.

75
00:04:21.271 --> 00:04:24.065
A, ever. B, never. C, yet.

76
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.739
The answer is B: never.

77
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:32.883
She has blank to Japan twice.

78
00:04:33.183 --> 00:04:36.163
A, been. B, gone. C, be.

79
00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.374
The answer is A: been.

80
00:04:42.517 --> 00:04:44.203
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:44.503 --> 00:04:50.188
A, I haven't never tried it.. B, I have never tried it.. C, I never have tried not..

82
00:04:53.733 --> 00:04:56.383
The answer is B: I have never tried it..

83
00:04:57.517 --> 00:05:01.618
According to the reading, how many times has the brother been to Siem Reap?

84
00:05:01.918 --> 00:05:05.757
A, three times. B, once. C, twice.

85
00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.567
The answer is A: three times.

86
00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:15.849
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.845
What have you never done but want to try?

88
00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.197
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:29.497 --> 00:05:41.904
I have never flown in a plane, but I want to try it. I have travelled by bus and by boat, but never by air. I use have never + past participle to talk about experiences I have not had.

90
00:05:42.204 --> 00:05:44.389
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:45.283 --> 00:05:51.604
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect: ever and never plus past participle.

92
00:05:51.904 --> 00:05:55.996
Today's value is adventure. Try new things and explore safely.

93
00:05:56.296 --> 00:05:59.402
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:05:59.702 --> 00:06:02.737
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

